<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0020/tu_0044> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasClassOfRecommendation> <http://digistrucmed.org/ClassOfRecommendation_III> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0020/tu_0070> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasClassOfRecommendation> <http://digistrucmed.org/ClassOfRecommendation_I> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0020/tu_0042> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Patients requiring pacing at the time of tricuspid valve surgery. Transvalvular leads should be avoided and epicardial ventricular leads used. During tricuspid valve surgery, removal of pre-existing transvalvular leads should be considered and preferred over sewing-in the lead between the annulus and a bio-prosthesis or annuloplasty ring. In the case of an isolated tricuspid annuloplasty based on an individual risk-benefit analysis, a pre-existing right ventricular lead may be left in place without jailing it between ring and annulus." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0020/tu_0075/locator> <http://digistrucmed.org/headerPath> "Class: IIa" .
